       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks unsafe and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg \u00d7 4 = **6400 mg/day**. That's double the usual prescription maximum of 3200 mg/day, and most inpatient orders stay at or below 2400 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and heart problems. These risks are higher in hospitalized adults, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This may be a typo. Common orders that might have been intended:**\n- Ibuprofen **400 mg** PO four times daily (1600 mg/day). This is the likeliest match, since 1600 is the daily total.\n- Ibuprofen **600 mg** PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen **800 mg** PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n\nPlease tell me which dose you meant and I'll enter it. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. That said, I'd strongly suggest checking with pharmacy before giving a dose this high."
      }
