       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you've confirmed it, but I'm still not going to enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6400 mg/day). That's double the maximum labeled dose, and no standard guideline supports it for any indication. The risk of serious harm is high: GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular events. Because your confirmation came without a clinical reason, I can't treat this as a deliberate, justified exception.\n\n**Ways I can help right now:**\n- **Enter a standard dose instead:** 400 mg, 600 mg or 800 mg by mouth, three or four times daily, up to 3200 mg/day.\n- **Enter 800 mg four times daily (3200 mg/day):** This is the labeled maximum, and I can add a note asking pharmacy to review it.\n- **Look at other pain options:** If the pain isn't controlled at maximum-dose ibuprofen, adding acetaminophen or another drug class is usually safer than going above the NSAID ceiling.\n\nIf this dose comes from a specific protocol or a specialist's recommendation, it should go through pharmacy verification or attending sign-off. You can still enter it yourself through the normal order-entry process, where those checks happen.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
